<title>UK: UK's Clarke says will not play Santa or Scrooge.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says will not play Santa or Scrooge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday he would not play Santa Claus or Scrooge with his annual budget for 1997/8. &quot;This is not a reckless budget on tax or spending. In the run up to Christmas I am not going to play Santa Claus, but this year I do not have to play Scrooge either,&quot; he said in a speech to parliament on the 1997/98 budget.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
